            </div>
            <div type="intro">
                <p>Passage from the <hi rend="italic">Perfection of Wisdom Sutra on Humane
                        Kings</hi>, on the Nature of the Perfection of Wisdom</p>
                <p>The passage is drawn from the <hi rend="italic">Perfection of Wisdom Sutra on
                        Humane Kings Spoken by the Buddha</hi> (<hi rend="italic">Foshuo renwang
                        bore boluomi jing</hi> 佛說仁王般若波羅蜜經; T#245, 8: 825a-834a), a scripture
                    traditionally attributed to the translator Kumārajīva (鳩摩羅什; 344-413), but in
                    all likelihood compiled in China in the 470s, see <ref type="bibli" target="Orzech1998">74-78</ref>. A modern collated edition of the received
                    version of this passage is located at T#245, 8: 832c23-26. In this received
                    version the passage does not include the mention of King Prasenajit, but begins
                    simply “Great King” (<hi rend="italic">dawang</hi> 大王). This passage, which
                    likens the perfection of wisdom to a series of powerful talismanic objects, is
                    notable not simply because it does so—many texts employ similar metaphors—but
                    because some of these objects are rather distinctively Chinese.</p>
                <ab>
                    <abbr>PC</abbr>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div xml:lang="en">
                <p>The <persName corresp="zh-a1" key="bg0004" reg="Sakyamuni" type="Buddha" xml:id="en-a1">Buddha</persName> told <persName corresp="zh-a2" key="rh0003" reg="Prasenajit" type="emperor" xml:id="en-a2">King Prasenajit</persName>:
                    This Perfection of Wisdom is the spiritual root of the consciousness of all
                    Buddhas, bodhisattvas, and all beings. It is the father and mother of all kings.
                    It is also named the Spiritual Talisman, the Demon-Exorcising Pearl, the
                    Wish-Fulfilling Pearl, the State-Protecting Pearl, the Mirror of Heaven and
                    Earth, and the Dragon-Jewel Spirit King. <ptr target="note_en_1"/>
                </p>
            </div>
